{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"Amazon Bedrock expands support for Service Quotas - AWS","context":"Amazon Bedrock, a managed service for enterprise-grade access to high-performing foundation models from leading AI companies, now supports viewing inference quotas for the bedrock-mantle endpoint through AWS Service Quotas. This allows customers to track limits for the endpoint in a familiar way and gain visibility into the limits that apply to their workloads. The bedrock-mantle endpoint supports OpenAI Responses API, OpenAI Chat Completions API, and Anthropic Messages API, enabling customers to run existing OpenAI or Anthropic based applications on Amazon Bedrock with minimal code changes. AWS Service Quotas now exposes per-model input-tokens-per-minute and output-tokens-per-minute quotas for supported models on the endpoint. Customers can view their current quotas by opening the AWS Service Quotas console, choosing Amazon Bedrock, and searching for \"Bedrock Mantle\". To request an increase to any quotas, follow the standard Amazon Bedrock limit increase process. Service Quotas support for the bedrock-mantle endpoint is available in all AWS Regions where the endpoint is offered, including US East (N. Virginia, Ohio), US West (Oregon), Asia Pacific (Mumbai, Tokyo, Sydney, Jakarta), Europe (Frankfurt, Ireland, London, Milan, Stockholm), and South America (São Paulo)","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/5/amazon-bedrock-service-quotas/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"Amazon Bedrock adds support for the latest open-weight models in Asia Pacific (Sydney) - AWS","context":"Amazon Bedrock, a managed service offering secure access to high-performance foundation models from leading AI companies, has announced support for the latest open-weight models in Asia Pacific (Sydney) via the bedrock-mantle endpoint. The endpoint is powered by Project Mantle, a new distributed inference engine for large-scale machine learning model serving on Amazon Bedrock. Supported providers include DeepSeek, Google, MiniMax, Mistral, Moonshot AI, Nvidia, and OpenAI. Project Mantle simplifies model onboarding, provides performant and reliable serverless inference, offers sophisticated quality of service controls, and delivers OpenAI API compatibility out-of-the-box. To learn more and get started, visit the Amazon Bedrock console or service documentation, and for OpenAI API-compatible service endpoints, refer to the OpenAI API compatibility documentation","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/02/amazon-bedrock-support-latest-open-weight-models-asia-pacific-sydney/"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"Amazon Bedrock expands support for AWS PrivateLink - AWS","context":"Amazon Bedrock, a managed service for secure access to high-performing foundation models from leading AI companies, has expanded its support for AWS PrivateLink. This expansion includes the bedrock-mantle endpoint, which is powered by Project Mantle, a new distributed inference engine for large-scale machine learning model serving on Amazon Bedrock. With AWS PrivateLink, users can privately access their applications using the bedrock-mantle endpoint. Project Mantle simplifies and expedites onboarding of new models onto Amazon Bedrock, providing highly performant and reliable serverless inference, sophisticated quality of service controls, automated capacity management, and unified pools, as well as out-of-the-box compatibility with OpenAI API specifications. AWS PrivateLink support for OpenAI API-compatible endpoints is available in multiple AWS Regions, including US East (N. Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon), Asia Pacific (Jakarta), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), Asia Pacific (Mumbai), Asia Pacific (Sydney), South America (São Paulo), Europe (Frankfurt), Europe (Ireland), Europe (London), Europe (Milan), Europe (Stockholm), and South America (Sao Paulo). To learn more and get started, users can visit the Amazon Bedrock console or service documentation, and the OpenAI API compatibility documentation for Amazon Bedrock","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/02/amazon-bedrock-expands-aws-privatelink-support-openai-api-endpoints/"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"Amazon Bedrock adds Amazon CloudWatch metrics for OpenAI- and Anthropic-compatible APIs - AWS","context":"Amazon Bedrock, a managed service for secure access to high-performance AI models, now supports monitoring inference traffic to the bedrock-mantle endpoint using Amazon CloudWatch metrics. The endpoint is compatible with OpenAI Responses API, OpenAI Chat Completions API, and Anthropic Messages API, enabling minimal code changes for existing applications. Metrics include inference counts, input and output token totals, and client error counts, published at various granularity levels. Customers can monitor production inference, set up alarms, and plan capacity. The CloudWatch metrics are available in multiple AWS regions and can be accessed via the CloudWatch console","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/06/amazon-bedrock-supports-cloudwatch-metrics-bedrock-mantle-endpoint/"},{"rank_order":5,"title":"amazon-bedrock","skill_description":"Builds generative AI applications on Amazon Bedrock. Covers model invocation (Converse API, InvokeModel), RAG with Knowledge Bases, Bedrock Agents, Guardrails, and AgentCore (including the Harness managed agent loop). Applies when invoking models, setting up or migrating Knowledge Bases to Managed, deploying to AgentCore, migrating/porting/converting a Bedrock Agent (including inline agents) to an AgentCore Harness, troubleshooting Bedrock errors (ThrottlingException, AccessDeniedException), or choosing Bedrock models (Claude, Llama, Nova, Titan). Also for prompt caching, quota and throttling diagnosis, cost tracking, migrating between Claude model generations, chunking strategies, and Bedrock model selection. Covers AgentCore Payments (x402, microtransactions, Payment Manager, Connector, Instrument, Coinbase CDP, Stripe Privy, paid endpoints, agent payments). NOT for custom model training, Rekognition, or Comprehend. For SageMaker model discovery, customization, or endpoints, use aws-ai-ml.\n\nServices: bedrock, bedrock-runtime, bedrock-mantle, bedrock-agent, bedrock-agent-runtime, bedrock-agentcore-control, bedrock-agentcore\nTasks: deploy, debug, optimize, design, migrate\nPersona: developer, devops, architect\nWorkload: generative-ai, rag, agents","skill_name":"amazon-bedrock"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Search docs on bedrock-mantle endpoint and Mantle"}
